{"conversation":"tomcat","question":"What engines does the F-14B have?","reply":{"answer":"The F-14B is powered by two General Electric F110-GE-400 engines, each providing 27,000 lb of thrust [1, 2].","ids":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","title":"F-14 Tomcat"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles","title":"F-14 Tomcat · Swing wings and Phoenix missiles"}]},"ms":2206,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"tomcat","question":"And the A model?","reply":{"answer":"The F-14A is powered by two Pratt & Whitney TF30-P-414A afterburning turbofans, each providing 20,900 lb of thrust [1].","ids":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","title":"F-14 Tomcat"}]},"ms":1282,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
