{"conversation":"sochi","question":"What freq is Sochi tower?","reply":{"answer":"In DCS: Caucasus, the Sochi-Adler tower frequencies are 127.0 MHz VHF, 256.0 MHz UHF, 39.6 MHz low VHF, and 4.05 MHz HF.","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","title":"Sochi-Adler · DCS: Caucasus"}]},"ms":1455,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"sochi","question":"Does it have a TACAN?","reply":{"answer":"In DCS: Caucasus, the Sochi-Adler airfield has an NDB with marker (CO) and an ILS on runway 06, but a TACAN is not listed in the simulator record.","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","title":"Sochi-Adler · DCS: Caucasus"}]},"ms":834,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"sochi","question":"What about ILS?","reply":{"answer":"In DCS: Caucasus, there is an ILS on runway 06 at 111.1 MHz (ISO).","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#facilities-title"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","title":"Sochi-Adler · DCS: Caucasus"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#facilities-title","title":"Sochi International Airport · Runways and facilities"}]},"ms":1102,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"sochi","question":"What runways are available?","reply":{"answer":"The real-world airport has runways 06/24 and 02/20, but DCS: Caucasus only has runway 06/24, which is listed with headings of 059 and 239 respectively.","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/","/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#sims-title","/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#facilities-title"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/","title":"Sochi International Airport"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#sims-title","title":"Sochi International Airport · Sim maps"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-caucasus/#af-sochi-adler","title":"Sochi-Adler · DCS: Caucasus"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/sochi/#facilities-title","title":"Sochi International Airport · Runways and facilities"}]},"ms":1775,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"ramat","question":"What is the TACAN for Ramat David?","reply":{"answer":"In DCS: Sinai, the TACAN is VORTAC 84X, 113.7 MHz (RMD); in DCS: Syria, the TACAN is VORTAC 84X, 113.7 MHz (RMD).","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/ramat-david/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Sinai"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Syria"}]},"ms":2109,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"ramat","question":"What runways are available?","reply":{"answer":"In DCS: Sinai, the available runways are 09 (082°) / 27 (262°), 11 (103°) / 29 (283°), and 15 (140°) / 33 (320°). In DCS: Syria, the available runways are 09 (082°) / 27 (262°), 11 (103°) / 29 (283°), and 33 (320°) / 15 (140°). In Falcon BMS: Israel, the runways are 09/27, 11/29, and 15/33.","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david","/encyclopedia/locations/ramat-david/#sims-title"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/ramat-david/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Sinai"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Syria"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/ramat-david/#sims-title","title":"Ramat David Airbase · Sim maps"}]},"ms":3791,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"ramat","question":"Which one runs east-west?","reply":{"answer":"None of the runways at Ramat David run east-west; the available runways are oriented approximately east-west (09/27 at 082°/262°), northeast-southwest (11/29 at 103°/283°), and southeast-northwest (15/33 at 140°/320°).","ids":["/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/locations/ramat-david/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-sinai/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Sinai"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/locations/dcs-syria/#af-ramat-david","title":"Ramat David · DCS: Syria"}]},"ms":2240,"passed":false,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
