{"conversation":"concepts","question":"What is angle of attack?","reply":{"answer":"Angle of attack is the angle formed by the chord of an airfoil and the direction of the relative wind or between the chord line and the flight path.","ids":["/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/terminology/#aoa","title":"AOA"}]},"ms":686,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"concepts","question":"What is a VORTAC?","reply":{"answer":"A VORTAC is a ground navigation aid that provides VOR azimuth, TACAN azimuth, and TACAN distance using paired VHF and UHF bands. Because the VOR and TACAN channels are paired, a TACAN-equipped aircraft receives distance from the station automatically.","ids":["/manual/navigation/air-navigation/#navaids"],"topic":[],"references":[{"id":"/manual/navigation/air-navigation/#navaids","title":"Air Navigation · Radio navigation aids"}]},"ms":1541,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
{"conversation":"tomcat-alias","question":"What engines does the Tomcat have?","reply":{"answer":"The F-14A uses two Pratt & Whitney TF30-P-414A afterburning turbofans, while the F-14B and F-14D use two General Electric F110-GE-400 engines.","ids":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles"],"topic":["/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/"],"references":[{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/","title":"F-14 Tomcat"},{"id":"/encyclopedia/aircraft/f-14/#swing-wings-and-phoenix-missiles","title":"F-14 Tomcat · Swing wings and Phoenix missiles"}]},"ms":1848,"passed":true,"revision":"4a624fd75a4bc64720c9780a5854e832cd75ebde"}
